A||||2||Terrybogin||Are we also them???||||1||
Z||000000||Terrybogin||05-05-2000||01:02 AM||||Going to work this morning, traffic is really moving slow in the left lane. I finally get a chance to jump over a couple of lanes and see what the hold up is. Turns out the slow car was a new 'Vette. It seems that most people with high power cars drive them like paw-paw drove the tractor. Then at the redlight, some kid in a v6 mustang acts like he wants to race the 'Vette. <BR>Question: All these Riced out mini-motored cars going fast, high powered cars going slow. Where do we fit into this equation? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shiner||05-05-2000||01:20 AM||||One of the most wonderfull things about the Fiero is that there is no stereotype for Fiero drivers.  I have seen just about every type of person driving one.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||05-05-2000||08:42 AM||||Put me in the low-power, fast-driving category.  <P>There's nothing worse than a high performance car poking along in the left lane - then when you try to pass on the right, he speeds up to race you.  I don't want to race - I just want to get to work on time!||||reg||1
